\item \code{'Glia-In'} (Intrinsic): Measures cell-intrinsic aging of \strong{Glial cells}.
(Uses processed data: residuals/Z-scores).
\item \code{'Neu-Sin'} (Semi-intrinsic): Measures aging of \strong{Neurons} using raw data.
(Reflects both intrinsic aging and composition changes).
\item \code{'Glia-Sin'} (Semi-intrinsic): Measures aging of \strong{Glial cells} using raw data.
(Reflects both intrinsic aging and composition changes).
\item \code{'Hep'} (Semi-intrinsic): Measures aging of \strong{Hepatocytes} using raw data.
}

\strong{2. Non Cell-Type Specific Clocks}
\itemize{
\item \code{'Brain'} (Intrinsic): A intrinsic clock for \strong{whole brain tissue}.
